193
00:12:10,220 --> 00:12:12,320
Come on, we set sail in a few days.

194
00:12:12,740 --> 00:12:14,740
I don't want us to part like this.

195
00:12:28,860 --> 00:12:31,440
How dare you show your face here?

196
00:12:31,800 --> 00:12:34,741
Do you want your wife to
live her life as a widow?

197
00:12:44,240 --> 00:12:46,800
The Commodore seems sad lately.

198
00:12:48,260 --> 00:12:49,720
Yeah, it's unfortunate.

199
00:12:50,080 --> 00:12:52,845
He thought he made such
a good friend out here.

200
00:12:55,320 --> 00:12:57,360
None of this makes any sense.

201
00:12:58,160 --> 00:13:02,037
It looks like we're going to set
sail first thing tomorrow morning.

202
00:13:02,120 --> 00:13:04,917
The villagers are so upset
that we can't go near them.

203
00:13:05,000 --> 00:13:08,294
Plus, I don't remember ever
hearing the bell ring today.

204
00:13:11,660 --> 00:13:14,260
How dare you show your face here!

205
00:13:14,560 --> 00:13:17,501
Do you want your wife to
live her life as a widow?

206
00:13:33,960 --> 00:13:37,360
I gotta say, this is definitely
a tough way to leave.

207
00:13:41,640 --> 00:13:42,470
Idiot!

208
00:13:42,553 --> 00:13:44,520
Why did I believe he was a botanist?

209
00:13:50,660 --> 00:13:52,240
Damn you, Noland!

210
00:13:52,860 --> 00:13:56,440
If these are the unfortunate
victims of your advancement,

211
00:13:56,780 --> 00:14:01,100
