in search of revenge.

227
00:14:53,460 --> 00:14:55,517
We must drive them off this island!

228
00:14:55,600 --> 00:14:56,430
Alright!

229
00:14:58,960 --> 00:15:01,697
But because you had already saved so many

230
00:15:01,780 --> 00:15:06,660
lives here they couldn't just I understand

231
00:15:08,160 --> 00:15:11,137
They were so grateful
that they couldn't act

232
00:15:11,220 --> 00:15:14,577
on it but doctor even
if it was just for tree

233
00:15:14,660 --> 00:15:18,777
Research even if you
didn't know the villagers

234
00:15:18,860 --> 00:15:23,240
anger won't go away so
before you go I thought

235
00:15:24,360 --> 00:15:25,397
I'd ask. I...

236
00:15:25,480 --> 00:15:28,740
I have to know the reason why.

237
00:15:32,360 --> 00:15:35,007
So their ancestor spirits
are in those trees.

238
00:15:35,300 --> 00:15:37,065
I can't believe I didn't know.

239
00:15:37,840 --> 00:15:40,397
And now we've done something
terrible that we can't reverse.

240
00:15:40,480 --> 00:15:43,317
They have every right to
be as angry as they are.

241
00:15:43,400 --> 00:15:45,720
But, Commodore, we had no choice...

242
00:15:46,420 --> 00:15:47,497
There are no excuses.

243
00:15:47,580 --> 00:15:51,404
I was too wrapped up in my own
interests to even consider theirs.

244
00:15:53,940 --> 00:15:57,880
I was told that besides
proclaiming the city's existence,

245
00:15:58,300 --> 00:16:03,560
the Bell also served as a guide for
their ancestors to return to the island.

246
00:16:04,780 --> 00:16:06,660
And we just cut them down.

247
00:16:07,160 --> 00:16:09,360
We do not deserve their forgiveness.

248
00:16:10,380 --> 00:16:11,600
Commodore, wait.

249
00:16:13,940 --> 00:16:16,800
You want us to leave the treasure behind?

250
00:16:18,420 --> 00:16:22,067
