tree to people, and killed the island?

255
00:16:51,900 --> 00:16:54,076
What if you knew about it beforehand?

256
00:16:54,740 --> 00:16:56,177
What are you talking about?

257
00:16:56,260 --> 00:16:57,657
Please, tell us what you mean.

258
00:16:57,740 --> 00:16:59,300
If we had a choice,

259
00:17:00,820 --> 00:17:02,938
what would we do with that one tree?

260
00:17:04,820 --> 00:17:06,360
What would we do?

261
00:17:09,460 --> 00:17:10,500
Father, listen.

262
00:17:10,840 --> 00:17:13,000
You have to stop them. You fool.

263
00:17:13,260 --> 00:17:15,037
Don't you understand what they've done?

264
00:17:15,120 --> 00:17:16,777
We can't leave things this way.

265
00:17:16,860 --> 00:17:18,272
We'll regret it forever.

266
00:17:18,440 --> 00:17:20,740
You finally made such a dear friend.

267
00:17:21,140 --> 00:17:23,280
And we owe them so much!

268
00:17:23,760 --> 00:17:26,466
Father, we can't leave
them hurting like this!

269
00:17:26,560 --> 00:17:28,240
What are you talking about?

270
00:17:31,440 --> 00:17:35,381
There is no excuse, but on the
Commodore's behalf, I must say this.

271
00:17:35,500 --> 00:17:39,206
Those woods were already dead
before we arrived on this island.

272
00:17:39,500 --> 00:17:43,497
The worst thing about tree fever
is that it also infects plant life.

273
00:17:43,580 --> 00:17:48,286
Commodore Noland understood this, and
that was his reason for doing what he did.

274
00:17:48,680 --> 00:17:52,739
This is also why he pleaded with
you without regard for his own life.

275
00:17:55,000 --> 00:17:57,760
From people to forest
and forest to people,

276
00:17:58,100 --> 00:18:01,982
several small islands have been
destroyed in exactly the same way.

277
00:18:02,240 --> 00:18:03,540
Killed by fever.

278
00:18:05,600 --> 00:18:07,659
But there's nothing to worry about.

279
00:18:08,640 --> 00:18:11,993
Yesterday, we finished inspecting
the rest of the forest.

280
00:18:12,120 --> 00:18:14,497
I'm sorry we cut down your
forest without knowing,

281
00:18:14,580 --> 00:18:17,617
and I feel worse that we
never explained why we did it.

282
00:18:17,700 --> 00:18:21,080
It's probably unforgivable,
even with an explanation.

283
00:18:21,440 --> 00:18:25,028
But a botanist would never harm
a forest without good reason.

284
00:18:26,260 --> 00:18:30,378
Trust me, the Commodore doesn't have
anything against gods or spirits.

285
00:18:32,860 --> 00:18:35,497
It's just that he always
has to make a choice,

286
00:18:35,580 --> 00:18:38,280
and he always knows
what is most important.

287
00:18:40,340 --> 00:18:44,281
So, that means that they did all
of that to try to help our people?

288
00:18:49,260 --> 00:18:50,090
Father!

289
00:18:52,760 --> 00:18:54,340
I'm sorry, Noland.

290
00:18:54,720 --> 00:18:56,400
Please don't leave yet.

291
00:18:57,880 --> 00:18:59,680
Does everyone have everything?

292
00:19:00,340 --> 00:19:01,640
Not everything.

293
00:19:02,080 --> 00:19:03,280
You wuss.

294
00:19:04,680 --> 00:19:06,974
All right, everyone, to your positions.

295
00:19:07,100 --> 00:19:08,357
It's time to set sail.

296
00:19:08,440 --> 00:19:10,997
We're now on our way back
to the Levineal Kingdom.

297
00:19:11,080 --> 00:19:11,910
Yeah!

298
00:19:14,320 --> 00:19:15,150
Noland!

299
00:19:15,960 --> 00:19:18,757
I can't believe I made such a mistake.

300
00:19:18,840 --> 00:19:21,300
Nolan, wait!

301
00:19:24,740 --> 00:19:26,380
Set sail.

302
00:19:35,140 --> 00:19:39,160
The bell why would it be ringing now?

303
00:19:42,700 --> 00:19:43,980
Sorry, Nolan

304
00:19:45,040 --> 00:19:45,920
Ring louder!

305
00:19:46,320 --> 00:19:48,791
Nolan and the rest of them can't hear you!

306
00:19:51,340 --> 00:19:52,840
Look over there!

307
00:20:02,760 --> 00:20:04,180
Wait, Nolan!

308
00:20:06,100 --> 00:20:08,340
Is that you, Kalgara?

309
00:20:22,120 --> 00:20:23,080
Come back!

310
00:20:30,120 --> 00:20:32,820
Come back, please, Noland, you've got to!

311
00:20:34,820 --> 00:20:37,977
I'll ring the bell so you
can find your way back to us!

312
00:20:38,060 --> 00:20:42,417
I don't want you to lose sight
of this island, because one day!

313
00:20:42,500 --> 00:20:45,717
I want you to return my dear friend!

314
00:20:45,800 --> 00:20:47,397
Nolan!

315
00:20:47,480 --> 00:20:49,940
please come back!

316
00:20:59,900 --> 00:21:02,557
I know we'll meet again?

317
00:21:02,640 --> 00:21:03,717
someday Nolan!

318
00:21:03,800 --> 00:21:06,100
have a safe voyage.

319
00:21:09,200 --> 00:21:10,080
so

320
00:21:10,940 --> 00:21:12,820
I can't come back again.

321
00:21:16,880 --> 00:21:18,360
Of course I will.

322
00:21:18,640 --> 00:21:20,180
I'll come back.

323
00:21:24,900 --> 00:21:26,400
Someday, Kalgana!

324
00:21:26,660 --> 00:21:28,220
I know we'll meet again!

325
00:21:40,840 --> 00:21:44,537
I can always hear your voice.

326
00:21:44,620 --> 00:21:47,177
While you wander far from home!

327
00:21:47,260 --> 00:21:49,697
Gazing out at the sky.

328
00:21:49,780 --> 00:21:52,457
You are just like the moon.

329
00:21:52,540 --> 00:21:57,080
You never change as you
climb into the night?

330
00:22:00,460 --> 00:22:03,937
But your reflection wanes.

331
00:22:04,020 --> 00:22:08,420
Then you disappear, fading so silently.

332
00:22:09,480 --> 00:22:12,257
Stay as you are.

333
00:22:12,340 --> 00:22:14,857
Don't lose your way!

334
00:22:14,940 --> 00:22:18,060
Let these words guide you.

335
00:22:19,560 --> 00:22:22,020
Don't ever look back!

336
00:22:24,060 --> 00:22:27,337
Don't give up on your dreams.

337
00:22:27,420 --> 00:22:28,697
They're endless nights.

338
00:22:28,780 --> 00:22:32,717
They come to you again and again?

339
00:22:32,800 --> 00:22:35,437
Until you see the journey through.

340
00:22:35,520 --> 00:22:41,337
You may not return, I
hope that you'll learn!

341
00:22:41,420 --> 00:22:46,880
To put your past behind,
and just keep moving on.
